{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729729Z","id":"afa8b528e7374450a20a041d28d29d75deae1d2b3e7525ce1dcdbfe7fecc4df4","body":{"detail":"Seen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970746Z","id":"e186fa5eb94b4d4745bc582f181edaca45f47ef4742794b12e457f31b20db499","body":{"detail":"check_person_name compares the token form only with the owner, connected unrevoked persons and live agents. Extending it to every viewer row breaks two behaviours the store tests pin: a revoked person's name is free again (people.rs revoking_a_grant_ends_its_sessions_and_revoking_a_person_keeps_history) and an unredeemed invite frees the name (an_unredeemed_invites_person_goes_back_to_a_viewer). With the rule unenforced, the old cookie of a revoked 'Mia', or a LAN viewer who named themselves 'Jun' before Jun was invited, comments under the same name as the connected person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":350},"end":{"line":375},"content_hash":"a1f8247d6233f381c1f7bd1582a76e16b34dc4494d83697c90b2ce355cfddd91"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether revoked and lapsed persons' rows count as existing viewers for §9.6; then either check all viewer rows (and rename or mark the older one) or amend §9.6.","summary":"A new person may take the name of an existing plain LAN viewer, a revoked person or an unredeemed invite's person, though spec §9.6 says a new person cannot be named after an existing viewer's name","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:9.6","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970963Z","id":"ebd868e7580dc68c488bfac1f17d29a446dfa3a85b3d30f8cb5b27099ac4a203","body":{"detail":"Spec §11 refuses naming a person to a live agent's name (409 name_taken), and §9.6 refuses viewers the owner's or a person's name, but set_owner_name only checks the name's form. Checking it would change single-owner behaviour that §19 does not list, so it is left as it was.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":389},"end":{"line":392},"content_hash":"6c717bdc42d7c2983ff9d8169636be81e1725987de1a1689ff487a84a0324a3c"},"summary":"The owner can rename themselves to a live agent's name or a connected person's name; nothing refuses it","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.971168Z","id":"a7e7b5c6856d3630e36f7641bb0f0bfc14b51dd7d43458726e7c0de07f385cc7","body":{"detail":"send_in skips every viewer comment that has a feedback row for any target, so POST …/threads/<tid>/send {to} after the thread went to another agent inserts no rows for the new one, though it becomes the thread's target. Store::send_to_named (used for @name) instead checks rows per target, so the two ways of sending to one agent differ.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":190},"content_hash":"fa071b0439a92e52e404930d6c2d65a5073dd91f44b9ab2dd0c480371df7f5f9"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether a send with to should, like @name, give the named agent every comment it has no row for (spec §12 makes it the thread's owner).","summary":"A send with to on a thread whose comments already have rows gives the named agent nothing","tags":["spec:12","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.122041Z","id":"6d73133464fbe924b4046f650e56047664681d4dbffa53ff8c285b63a56fcf62","body":{"detail":"Checking only viewers with no invites row (NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM invites WHERE viewer_id = v.id)) and not revoked keeps the two pinned behaviours (revoking_a_grant_ends_its_sessions_and_revoking_a_person_keeps_history, an_unredeemed_invites_person_goes_back_to_a_viewer), and stops a LAN viewer who named themselves 'Jun' first from sharing the name with the person Jun. The 409 should point the owner at inviting that viewer ({viewer}, spec section 6.2) instead. A lapsed {viewer} invitee's name also stays free under this rule.","kind":"comment","references":"e186fa5eb94b4d4745bc582f181edaca45f47ef4742794b12e457f31b20db499","summary":"Reviewer's recommendation: enforce section 9.6 against viewer rows no invite made, and keep revoked and lapsed invitees' names free","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.122080Z","id":"131f80f14301f0003a7c26ea2e76e3131a90b4d7d2b22f683e60b45815838a96","body":{"detail":"Section 11 reserves the owner's display name from agents and refuses a person a live agent's name; the reverse for the owner is the same rule. Without it the owner named 'web' makes '@web' both a mention of the owner and a send to the agent web, and an owner named 'Sam' shares a name with the person Sam in agents' author lines. In a single-owner install it refuses only a live agent's exact name, so the section 19 change is one line.","kind":"comment","references":"ebd868e7580dc68c488bfac1f17d29a446dfa3a85b3d30f8cb5b27099ac4a203","summary":"Reviewer's recommendation: refuse the owner a live agent's name or a connected person's token form (409 name_taken), and add it to spec section 19 item 8","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
